{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 RCA — CONFIRMED defect (deterministic reproduction, thread + cross-process)\n\n**Proven root cause.** `save_checkpoint` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py:756-771`) derives\nthe temp path as `tmp = d / f\".tmp-{envelope.digest}.json\"` in the per-ticket dir\n`_checkpoint_dir` = `.rebar/cache/plan-review/<ticket_id>` — a pathname keyed by (ticket, digest)\nONLY, not run-scoped/unique-per-writer. Two concurrent writers for the same (ticket, digest)\ntherefore target the SAME temp file: both `tmp.write_text(...)`, then both `tmp.replace(path)`.\nThe first replace consumes the shared temp inode; the second raises `FileNotFoundError`, which the\nouter `except Exception: return False` swallows — the losing writer silently returns `False` and\nits checkpoint is lost. This violates the function's own docstring invariant (\"Persist an envelope\nATOMICALLY (tmp + rename)\") and is the exact construct proven and fixed in sibling bug\n`7dea-2f00-db57-4a96` (completion_verdict_cache, Gerrit 2329, commit 89981d8e81fa), in a different\nsubsystem.\n\n**Proof (discriminating runtime experiments).**\n- *Thread case* — two `save_checkpoint` threads for the same ctx+digest, a barrier at the real\n  `pathlib.Path.replace` seam forcing both temp writes before either replace:\n  `results = {'B': True, 'A': False}`, final JSON valid (winner `from-B`), no `.tmp` residue.\n- *Exact exception captured* — the losing writer's second replace raises\n  `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../.tmp-<digest>.json' -> '.../<digest>.json'`,\n  confirming the shared-temp inode was consumed by the winner and the loss path is the\n  `except Exception -> return False` swallow.\n- *Cross-process case* — two `multiprocessing` processes writing the shared temp then racing the\n  replace under a filesystem barrier: `{'A': 'FileNotFoundError', 'B': 'True'}`, no residue —\n  identical collision at the filesystem layer, proving it is not a thread/GIL artifact.\n\nPredicted-if-true (a concurrent writer returns False / raises FileNotFoundError at the second\nreplace) observed; predicted-if-false (both return True) rejected. This discriminates the shared\ndeterministic-temp mechanism from any per-writer-unique-temp alternative.\n\n**Legitimacy = defect.** Cited authorities: (1) the `save_checkpoint` docstring's ATOMIC\ntmp+rename invariant, which the shared temp breaks under concurrency; (2) prior closed `Fixed:`\nbug `7dea-2f00-db57-4a96` for the identical construct class (a defect there → a defect here).\n\n**Caller-dependency gate → clear (only-incidental).** The sole caller,\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:358`, is inside a Pass-1 discovery thread-pool fan-out (up to\n6 workers) and **ignores** the boolean return. The fix (unique per-writer temp, same atomic\nreplace onto the shared final key) is behaviour-preserving for that caller: no contract, schema,\nor output change. Concurrency is real — the fan-out is threaded, and two concurrent plan-review\nruns for the same ticket share the ticket-keyed dir.\n\n**Defect origin (attribution).** The shared-deterministic-temp construct\n(`tmp = d / f\".tmp-{key}.json\"` + `tmp.replace(path)`) was FIRST introduced when `save_checkpoint`\nwas created in commit `01ab667e4079` (\"feat(plan-review): chunk-atomic checkpointing + extract\nsizing.py\", 2026-06-24), under epic `5fd2-a7c2-0aec-48fa` (\"Plan-review verification gate\nopen->in_progress\" — the commit body states it remediates that epic's remaining ACs). Commit\n`e422395a18be` (\"Journal plan-review discovery via shared kernel\", ticket cfb7, a story) is a\nCARRIER: it re-keyed the temp from `{key}` to `{envelope.digest}` but preserved the shared-temp\nbug; `git blame -w -C -M` on lines 766-767 names it, but walking back through it reaches the true\norigin `01ab667`. `01ab667` predates the `rebar-ticket:` trailer convention (no trailer/subject\nid), so attribution is by SCOPE-OF-WORK to epic `5fd2`, which scoped chunk-atomic checkpointing.\nClass = `plan_defect` (the originating plan specified a shared deterministic temp), matching the\n`7dea` precedent (closed `plan_defect`). Close will carry\n`--class=plan_defect --caused-by=5fd2-a7c2-0aec-48fa`.\n\n**Duplicates.** `6485-fd81-5f58-4f55` (open bug, identical title, created ~26s before this ticket)\nis the same defect — linked `d284 duplicates 6485`. This fix resolves both."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787946352846958001,"uuid":"0c1f90e2-c2e4-44c7-9ea0-5c65f77d79f1"}